+      },
+      {
+        "id": "level_on_frame_not_game",
+        "note": "level = frame.levels_completed; env._game has no levels_completed."
+      },
+      {
+        "id": "deepcopy_injection_unreliable",
+        "note": "env._game=deepcopy(state) works for lp85, BROKEN for sc25; use replay-from-reset."
+      },
+      {
+        "id": "first_step_after_reset_consumed",
+        "note": "first env.step after reset is a no-op (sc25); warm up after reset."
+      },
+      {
+        "id": "discover_coords_never_hardcode",
+        "note": "live-coupled hardcoded coords miss the offline layout; discover from env."
+      },
+      {
+        "id": "state_dependent_controls_and_animations",
+        "note": "tank-controls facing + multi-frame animations; include facing/phase in the dedup key and resolve animations before win-check."
+      },
+      {
+        "id": "non_idempotent_reset",
+        "note": "gotcha #7 (tu93): env.reset() is NOT idempotent -- it leaves a parity-toggling hidden state (same path, 6 reset+replays -> levels [1,2,1,2,1,2]). A reuse-one-env replay/deepcopy search detects parity-CONTINGENT wins that fail the fresh-env reproduction gate (gate correctly rejects -- no false claim). Fix: OfflineSolver branch_mode='fresh_env' (a brand-new env per candidate eval) so each evaluation sees the same pristine parity-0 the gate uses. Detect by replaying ONE path on N fresh envs vs 1 env reset N times: if levels differ, reset is non-idempotent."
+      },
+      {
+        "id": "same_action_next_level",
+        "note": "Some config/toggle games call next_level() in the same action that creates the winning arrangement, so the returned frame is already the next level and the pre-win grid is not externally observable. Ground the win predicate on execution state immediately before next_level, then count only the reproduce() level advance."
